# ⚔️ Win Conditions

## 🧊 Classic Mode

Classic Mode will use the original **Frozen Giant Showdown** concept as its complete starting gameplay foundation.

The source win structure includes:

- 🗿 Giant Frozen Yeti with 1000 HP
- 👤 Tiny/Survivor Players completing Frozen Parkour
- 🎯 Reaching the Cannon Area
- 💥 Cannon hits dealing 25 damage
- 🎯 40 successful hits required to reduce 1000 HP to 0
- ⏳ Time expiration as the original Giant-side win condition

These numbers belong to the Classic Mode source concept and do not automatically become universal rules for every future GIANTBOUND mode.

## 🧊 Classic Mode Gameplay Structure

The Classic Mode flow can use the original sequence:

**🧗 Frozen Parkour → 🎯 Cannon Area → 💥 Attack Giant → 🏁 Result**

The Giant uses environmental control, obstacles, powers, and disruption to make the Tiny/Survivor route harder.

## 🔮 Future Modes

Future modes can have completely different win conditions. GIANTBOUND should not force every mode to use Giant HP, cannon damage, or the same objective.

Possible future modes may use:

- 🎯 Objective completion
- 🏁 Race/progression
- ⚔️ Team battles
- 🛡️ Survival conditions
- 💥 Boss-style Giant battles
- 💡 New original win systems

These are discussion directions only.

## ⚖️ Design Requirement

Whatever the mode, both sides should have meaningful gameplay and a clear reason to act. A mode should make the Giant/Tiny relationship the center of its win condition rather than using a passive timer alone.
